{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport sys\ninput = sys.stdin.readline\n\ndef make_seg_tree(n):\n    size = 1\n    while size < n:\n        size <<= 1\n    return [0] * (size << 1)\n\ndef seg_set(tree, idx, val):\n    pos = idx + len(tree) // 2\n    tree[pos] = val\n    pos >>= 1\n    while pos:\n        tree[pos] = tree[pos << 1] + tree[(pos << 1) + 1]\n        pos >>= 1\n\ndef seg_get(tree, l, r):\n    l += len(tree) // 2\n    r += len(tree) // 2\n    res = 0\n    while l <= r:\n        if l & 1:\n            res += tree[l]\n            l += 1\n        if not (r & 1):\n            res += tree[r]\n            r -= 1\n        l >>= 1\n        r >>= 1\n    return res\n\ndef factorization(n):\n    res = []\n    d = 2\n    while d * d <= n:\n        while n % d == 0:\n            res.append(d)\n            n //= d\n        d += 1\n    if n > 1:\n        res.append(n)\n    return res\n\ndef phi_func(n):\n    primes = set(factorization(n))\n    val = n\n    for p in primes:\n        val = val // p * (p - 1)\n    return val\n\ndef range_mult(a, b, m):\n    prod = 1\n    for i in range(a + 1, b + 1):\n        prod = (prod * i) % m\n    return prod\n\nn, mod = map(int, input().split())\nphi_mod = phi_func(mod)\narr_len = n + 5\nfacts = [1] * (arr_len + 1)\nfor i in range(1, arr_len + 1):\n    facts[i] = (i * facts[i - 1]) % mod\n\nif n <= 3:\n    print(0)\nelse:\n    dp = [0] * 2000\n    dp[0], dp[1], dp[2], dp[3] = 1, 2, 2, 1\n    seg = make_seg_tree(2005)\n    for i in range(4):\n        seg_set(seg, i, dp[i])\n    max_idx = 3\n    total = 0\n    for step in range(n - 3):\n        old_dp = dp[:]\n        sub_sum = 0\n        for j in range(step + 3):\n            for k in range(1, max_idx + 2):\n                s = seg_get(seg, j + k + 1, 2004)\n                sub_sum = (sub_sum + s * old_dp[k - 1]) % mod\n                dp[j + k] = (dp[j + k] + old_dp[k - 1]) % mod\n                seg_set(seg, j + k, dp[j + k])\n        max_idx += step + 3\n        mult = range_mult(step + 3, n, mod)\n        total = (total + mult * sub_sum) % mod\n    print(total)\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static BufferedReader br;\n    static PrintWriter out;\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        out = new PrintWriter(System.out);\n        \n        String[] line = br.readLine().split(\" \");\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(line[0]);\n        int mod = Integer.parseInt(line[1]);\n        \n        int phi_mod = phi_func(mod);\n        int arr_len = n + 5;\n        long[] facts = new long[arr_len + 1];\n        facts[0] = 1;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= arr_len; i++) {\n            facts[i] = (i * facts[i - 1]) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        if (n <= 3) {\n            out.println(0);\n            out.close();\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        long[] dp = new long[2000];\n        dp[0] = 1;\n        dp[1] = 2;\n        dp[2] = 2;\n        dp[3] = 1;\n        \n        long[] seg = make_seg_tree(2005);\n        for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n            seg_set(seg, i, dp[i]);\n        }\n        \n        int max_idx = 3;\n        long total = 0;\n        \n        for (int step = 0; step < n - 3; step++) {\n            long[] old_dp = Arrays.copyOf(dp, dp.length);\n            long sub_sum = 0;\n            \n            for (int j = 0; j < step + 3; j++) {\n                for (int k = 1; k <= max_idx + 2; k++) {\n                    long s = seg_get(seg, j + k + 1, 2004);\n                    sub_sum = (sub_sum + s * old_dp[k - 1]) % mod;\n                    dp[j + k] = (dp[j + k] + old_dp[k - 1]) % mod;\n                    seg_set(seg, j + k, dp[j + k]);\n                }\n            }\n            \n            max_idx += step + 3;\n            long mult = range_mult(step + 3, n, mod);\n            total = (total + mult * sub_sum) % mod;\n        }\n        \n        out.println(total);\n        out.close();\n    }\n    \n    static long[] make_seg_tree(int n) {\n        int size = 1;\n        while (size < n) {\n            size <<= 1;\n        }\n        return new long[size << 1];\n    }\n    \n    static void seg_set(long[] tree, int idx, long val) {\n        int pos = idx + tree.length / 2;\n        tree[pos] = val;\n        pos >>= 1;\n        while (pos > 0) {\n            tree[pos] = tree[pos << 1] + tree[(pos << 1) + 1];\n            pos >>= 1;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    static long seg_get(long[] tree, int l, int r) {\n        l += tree.length / 2;\n        r += tree.length / 2;\n        long res = 0;\n        while (l <= r) {\n            if ((l & 1) == 1) {\n                res += tree[l];\n                l += 1;\n            }\n            if ((r & 1) == 0) {\n                res += tree[r];\n                r -= 1;\n            }\n            l >>= 1;\n            r >>= 1;\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n    \n    static List<Integer> factorization(int n) {\n        List<Integer> res = new ArrayList<>();\n        int d = 2;\n        while (d * d <= n) {\n            while (n % d == 0) {\n                res.add(d);\n                n /= d;\n            }\n            d++;\n        }\n        if (n > 1) {\n            res.add(n);\n        }\n        return res;\n    }\n    \n    static int phi_func(int n) {\n        Set<Integer> primes = new HashSet<>(factorization(n));\n        int val = n;\n        for (int p : primes) {\n            val = val / p * (p - 1);\n        }\n        return val;\n    }\n    \n    static long range_mult(int a, int b, int m) {\n        long prod = 1;\n        for (int i = a + 1; i <= b; i++) {\n            prod = (prod * i) % m;\n        }\n        return prod;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00013004888023715466, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.0002037079248111695, -3.6238969187252223e-05, -0.5759837627410889, -0.5760838985443115, -0.0002494739310350269, -2.0503786799963564e-05, -9.97731985989958e-05, -0.0002411313180346042, -5.245195097813848e-06, -4.172316494077677e-06, -4.088794958079234e-05, -0.17975053191184998, -0.0006289887824095786, -0.6466847062110901, -0.13529498875141144, -0.0033147174399346113, -0.47416847944259644, -5.876845170860179e-05, -3.576272320060525e-06, -0.00988894421607256, -0.6965463757514954, -0.14267860352993011, -0.3132762908935547, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.033824991434812546, -1.4185804502631072e-05, -0.004108085297048092, -1.490105023549404e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -0.00011359999916749075, -1.7881233361549675e-05, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -0.00421172333881259, -0.012543829157948494, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -3.933898824470816e-06, -0.00034481301554478705, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -1.2636104656849056e-05, -7.664863369427621e-05, -5.686121585313231e-05, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -3.337854650453